Skip texture uploads that are stale or overwritten whole (Switch 2 titles), adapted from Lichii
(github.com/zortos293/Lichii) #818 and #817 in their final, corrected form. Ocarina of Time moves
its render targets from frame to frame and resizes a shadow map every frame in parts of Kokiri
Forest: the cache kept making new images there and uploaded guest memory first (stale bytes the GPU
overwrites, ~9 GB every 30 s; 4-7 MiB twice a frame for the shadow map).
Stale pages: when the collector drops a GPU-written image without writing it back, its guest memory
no longer holds the GPU's data. Only that deletion marks (not JoinImages' deletions, whose data
lives on in the new image), only on Switch 2 titles (g_nx2_ampere), never for a CpuModified, Sparse
or Unbacked image, and only the whole 4 KiB pages inside the image (StalePages, stale_pages.h). The
pages stay tracked (cached count +1); a CPU write, an unmap, an image write-back and a buffer
write-back (every device range GetSubmappedRange returns) clear every page they touch and release
the tracking. RefreshContents makes an image lying wholly on stale pages without an upload, unless
it is Sparse, Unbacked or Remapped or has dirty layers, or something other than an image wrote
there on the GPU. Upstream asks the buffer cache's Nx2MayBeGpuWritten for that; this core has no
such bitmap, and its GpuWrittenPages bitmap is also marked by every image write (including the
dropped image's own), which would make every stale page look written. GpuWrittenPages therefore
gets a second bitmap, non_image_bits, set by Mark (buffer cache, queries, semaphores, memory manager
writes: all of what upstream's bitmap holds and more, so never less conservative) and not by the new
MarkImage the texture cache's three image marks use; AnyNonImage reads it. The existing bitmap and
its readers (99zzzt1, 99zzzt2) behave as before.
Whole join copies: a new image that joins aliases was uploaded first and the alias copies ran on top
of it, oldest first. When one alias copy writes every texel (CopiesWriteWholeImage in util: same 2D
format and astc_opaque, every level and layer from the origin, 1x, no Rescaled, TrimmedLevels,
Unbacked or Sparse image on either side, no compressed format) the upload and the alias copies
before it are not made; the later copies, the non-alias copies and the clear case are unchanged.
The sort, alias bookkeeping and bad overlaps now precede the upload so the copies are known.
